# Favourites: a poem marked from its page is filed at the top of the shelf,
# survives a restart, and comes off again. A long poem turns its pages.
wait-for-id poem-menu
wait-idle 3000
tap Browse
wait-for Poems
expect-missing Favorites
tap-paged The Tiger
wait-for Tiger, tiger, burning bright
expect William Blake · 1794
# The Tiger is longer than one page at every size; the side turns it on and
# back, and the source line closes the last page.
expect-missing From Songs of Innocence
clean
shot tiger-first-page
tap-id poem-next
wait-idle
expect Did He who made the lamb make thee?
expect From Songs of Innocence and of Experience
clean
shot tiger-last-page
tap-id poem-previous
wait-idle
expect Could frame thy fearful symmetry?
# The heart is in the poem's panel, opened from the middle of the page, and
# fills when the poem is a favourite.
tap-id poem-menu
wait-for Make a quote card
tap Favorite
wait-idle
expect Remove favorite
clean
shot tiger-favourite
tap Back
wait-idle
tap Back
wait-for Favorites
expect The Tiger
clean
shot browse-favourites
# A favourite is written to the reader, so it is still there after a restart.
restart
wait-for-id poem-menu
wait-idle 3000
tap Browse
wait-for Favorites
expect The Tiger
# Removing it from the poem takes it off the shelf.
tap The Tiger
wait-for Tiger, tiger, burning bright
tap-id poem-menu
wait-for Make a quote card
tap Remove favorite
wait-idle
expect Favorite
tap Back
wait-idle
tap Back
wait-for Poems
expect-missing Favorites
# A favourite the reader would not write stays as it was: the banner says
# so, and the heart does not claim a change that was never kept.
tap-paged The Lamb
wait-for Little lamb, who made thee?
scenario storage-full
tap-id poem-menu
wait-for Make a quote card
tap Favorite
wait-for would not keep that favourite
expect-missing Remove favorite
clean
shot favourite-refused
scenario normal
